„­bible_version£KJV¤book.§chapter¨sections—…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQWould to God ye could bear with me a little in my folly: and indeed bear with me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹For I am jealous over you with godly jealousy: for I have espoused you to one husband, that I may present you as a chaste virgin to Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÒFor if he that cometh preacheth another Jesus, whom we have not preached, or if ye receive another spirit, which ye have not received, or another gospel, which ye have not accepted, ye might well bear with him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAFor I suppose I was not a whit behind the very chiefest apostles.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwBut though I be rude in speech, yet not in knowledge; but we have been throughly made manifest among you in all things.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€Have I committed an offence in abasing myself that ye might be exalted, because I have preached to you the gospel of God freely?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAI robbed other churches, taking wages of them, to do you service.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙúAnd when I was present with you, and wanted, I was chargeable to no man: for that which was lacking to me the brethren which came from Macedonia supplied: and in all things I have kept myself from being burdensome unto you, and so will I keep myself.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`As the truth of Christ is in me, no man shall stop me of this boasting in the regions of Achaia.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ/Wherefore? because I love you not? God knoweth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’But what I do, that I will do, that I may cut off occasion from them which desire occasion; that wherein they glory, they may be found even as we.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdFor such are false apostles, deceitful workers, transforming themselves into the apostles of Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGAnd no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Therefore it is no great thing if his ministers also be transformed as the ministers of righteousness; whose end shall be according to their works.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrI say again, Let no man think me a fool; if otherwise, yet as a fool receive me, that I may boast myself a little.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlThat which I speak, I speak it not after the Lord, but as it were foolishly, in this confidence of boasting.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:Seeing that many glory after the flesh, I will glory also.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:For ye suffer fools gladly, seeing ye yourselves are wise.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’For ye suffer, if a man bring you into bondage, if a man devour you, if a man take of you, if a man exalt himself, if a man smite you on the face.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒI speak as concerning reproach, as though we had been weak. Howbeit whereinsoever any is bold, (I speak foolishly,) I am bold also.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_Are they Hebrews? so am I. Are they Israelites? so am I. Are they the seed of Abraham? so am I.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™Are they ministers of Christ? (I speak as a fool) I am more; in labours more abundant, in stripes above measure, in prisons more frequent, in deaths oft.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9Of the Jews five times received I forty stripes save one.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThrice was I beaten with rods, once was I stoned, thrice I suffered shipwreck, a night and a day I have been in the deep;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙæin journeyings often, in perils of waters, in perils of robbers, in perils by mine own countrymen, in perils by the heathen, in perils in the city, in perils in the wilderness, in perils in the sea, in perils among false brethren;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqin weariness and painfulness, in watchings often, in hunger and thirst, in fastings often, in cold and nakedness.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdBeside those things that are without, that which cometh upon me daily, the care of all the churches.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@Who is weak, and I am not weak? who is offended, and I burn not?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQIf I must needs glory, I will glory of the things which concern mine infirmities.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcThe God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, which is blessed for evermore, knoweth that I lie not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyIn Damascus the governor under Aretas the king kept the city of the Damascenes with a garrison, desirous to apprehend me:¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSand through a window in a basket was I let down by the wall, and escaped his hands.¦